  "body": "## What happens\n\nA 3D Pocket level keeps the cutter centre one flute radius off the material above the level. The ladder does not look at the shank or the holder. Thus, beside a wall that is taller than the flute length, a shank that is wider than the flutes touches the wall. At a larger depth the holder touches the part too.\n\nThe generator reports the op as `ok`. Verify then names each such move as `shank_hit` (part) and each lift out of such a cut as `rapid_in_stock`. All of these findings have `blocks_post: true`, and `verify` holds the post by the op (`held_by`). Thus the output is not silent, but the user gets a toolpath that cannot post.\n\n## Evidence\n\nThe PR #1772 takeover found this (review 5910347140 of PR #1772).\n\n- The sample `testdata/models/sample_ap214.step` as imported, stock from the model, tool `EM-0600-4FL` (6 mm, 15 mm flute, 8 mm shank, 40 mm shank length, 44 mm holder). The part is 118 mm tall. 3D Pocket `R1` gives 306 `shank_hit` and 30 `rapid_in_stock`. All 30 rapids are vertical lifts up out of a cut. There is no gouge.\n- The same `R1` path (byte-identical moves) with `flute_len` 125 and `shank_d` 6 gives no findings and `ok: true`.\n- A closed cavity (40 mm block, 20 x 20 mm cavity, 30 mm deep, no open side) gives 121 `shank_hit` and 6 `rapid_in_stock` with the same tool. The result is the same with the footprint law of main (before #1749) and with the law of PR #1772. Thus the defect is on main.\n- #1840 reports the same kind of shank and holder findings for the 3D Finish `S1` on the same sample.\n- Pin: `crates/app/tests/shared_face_bodies.rs::the_sample_as_imported_roughs_the_3d_pocket_beside_its_silhouette` asserts this reading by name.\n\n## Workaround\n\nUse a tool whose flutes reach the full depth, with a shank that is not wider than the flutes. Or set Bottom Z to a depth that the tool reaches.\n\n## What to decide\n\nOne of these, by design:\n\n1. The ladder keeps the shank radius off the material above `level + flute_len`, and the holder radius off the material above `level + flute_len + shank_len`. Then the levels that the tool cannot reach are left as rest and named.\n2. The generator refuses the levels that the tool cannot reach, by name, before it builds the path.\n\nDo not change the verify laws. They are correct.\n\n## Done means\n\nA whole-model 3D Pocket with a tool that cannot reach the full depth beside a tall wall gives a path that verifies with no `shank_hit` and no `rapid_in_stock`, or a refusal or warning by name at generation. The pin in `shared_face_bodies.rs` changes to assert the new reading.\n",
